  "metadata": {
    "title": "The Screw-Pile Light",
    "description": "A screw-pile lighthouse: a little white keeper's house with its lantern on top, standing on iron legs over a rocky shoal out in the water. There is no bridge; the keeper comes and goes by the rowing boat moored under the ladder. Its lantern and windows light up after dark in World View. 27 bricks.\n\n## How it is built\n\nEach step is a group in the Editor, so you can select it, delete it or build it again yourself.\n\n1. **Shoal** — four dark Rocks in a square, one under each leg, and a fifth at the south side for a landing step.\n2. **Piles** — four dark Columns stand on the rocks and carry a timber Slab 4x4 well clear of the waves. White Beams make the railing round three sides (the side ones turned 90°, press **R**), and a Short Beam half of the fourth, leaving a gap at the top of the Ladder that climbs up from the landing rock.\n3. **Keeper's House** — a white Block 2x2 in the middle of the deck. The red Door faces the ladder; two Small Windows, turned 90°, look east and west and glow with lamplight at night.\n4. **Lantern** — a red Round Plate 2x2 on the roof, a Lantern that lights up after dark, another red Round Plate 2x2 and a red Cone Roof.\n5. **Boat** — a blue Plate 2x4 hull turned 90°, a Bench across it for the seat, and two Trims for oars, moored at the foot of the ladder.\n\nStand it out in open water, away from the shore, so the boat is the only way there.\n\n## Bricks\n\n- Shoal: 5 Rock\n- Piles: 4 Column, 1 Slab 4x4, 3 Beam, 1 Short Beam, 1 Ladder\n- Keeper's House: 1 Block 2x2, 1 Door, 2 Small Window\n- Lantern: 2 Round Plate 2x2, 1 Lantern, 1 Cone Roof\n- Boat: 1 Plate 2x4, 1 Bench, 2 Trim\n\n27 bricks in all.\n",
